WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:11.470
In an October 10 article in USA Today, Donald
Trump wrote that “If Democrats win control

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:17.710
of Congress this November, we will come dangerously
close to socialism in America.”

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.640
Are Americans embracing socialism?

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.970
In an August Fox News poll, 36 percent of
registered voters said it would be a good

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:30.670
thing for the US to move away from capitalism
and more toward socialism, while 51 percent

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:31.699
said it would be a bad thing.

00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:32.699
The new question shows more support for moving
away from capitalism than three earlier identical

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.699
questions that Fox has asked since 2010.

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:38.000
This summer Gallup also asked people about
their views of socialism and 37 percent said

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.120
they had a positive view, while 58 percent
had a negative one.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.940
In the September 2018 NBC News/Wall Street
Journal poll, 19 percent had a positive view

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:54.640
of socialism, 52 percent said they had a negative
view, and 26 percent a neutral one.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.100
In all of these polls, Democrats were more
positive about socialism than Republicans

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.760
and young people more so than older ones.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.480
Overall, though, Americans aren’t embracing
socialism.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.800
Do you think socialism would work in America?

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.460
Let us know in your comments.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:15.960
Also, let us know what other topics you’d
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.000
and be sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

